WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:09.968
Choose Design in A N C Studio and use the same brief box. Describe what you want, include the exact copy, and say how many designs you need.

2
00:00:10.568 --> 00:00:22.558
Add source files with the paperclip when you have them. The assistant also finds relevant visual references in the background. If an essential image is missing, it asks you for that content.

3
00:00:23.158 --> 00:00:35.174
Select Create the designs. The familiar creation sequence plans the requested outputs and generates the actual files. You can open the outline to review the plan before it continues.

4
00:00:35.774 --> 00:00:48.914
The result opens on the canvas. Use the arrows to compare designs and download the selected file. Refine adds a revised version alongside the original. Check the artwork before using it.

5
00:00:49.514 --> 00:00:59.179
For a proposal, choose Propose in the same place. Attach the request for proposal or pricing workbook, describe the presentation, and select Build the pitch.

6
00:00:59.779 --> 00:01:12.657
If the source needs clarification, creation pauses for your review. Check the display specifications, installation assumptions and source notes, then continue. The pitch follows the completed estimate.

7
00:01:13.257 --> 00:01:24.464
The result is a client presentation. Move through its pages or press Play for narration. Review the project scope and investment before presenting it to the client.

8
00:01:25.064 --> 00:01:36.375
Open Estimate beside the pitch to inspect the actual A N C P D F. Download the estimate for the client and the internal workbook for cost review. Generated prices remain budget estimates.

9
00:01:36.975 --> 00:01:48.364
Create a client link when you are ready to share the estimate. The link contains the P D F; source files and internal costs stay private. Revoke the link whenever access should end.

